# ${{skill.name}} — SharePoint / OneDrive as ${{config.account}} (${{config.title}})

Integration instance: `${{instance.name}}`. Always run the CLI with the instance flags:

`${{driver.python}} ${{driver.cli}} --cdp-url ${{config.cdp_url}} --account ${{config.account}} [--json] <command>`

Tokens are never printed; never echo them. If the user names another account/tenant, use that account's own skill.

## Commands
Library selection (per command, optional): `--site https://<tenant>.sharepoint.com/sites/<Name>` or `--drive b!<id>`; default is the own OneDrive. A **target** is a web/sharing URL, a ref (`f1`..) from the last `ls`/`search`, `<driveId>:<itemId>`, or a path like `/Recordings/call.vtt`.

| Need | Command |
|---|---|
| Identity, file scopes | `whoami` |
| Find sites / libraries | `sites [query] [--top N=25]`, `drives [--site S]` |
| List folder (prints refs f1..) | `ls [target=/] [--top N=50]` |
| Search files (name/content) | `search "words" [--top N=25]`, `recent`, `shared` |
| Metadata / versions | `info <target>`, `versions <target>` |
| Read content as text | `read <target> [--chars N=6000] [--full] [--timestamps]` — docx, pptx, xlsx, vtt, txt/md/csv/json |
| Read xlsx precisely | `read <target> --sheets` (sheets + used ranges), `read <target> --sheet S --range A1:H40 [--max-rows 50 --max-cols 20]` (compact table with column letters/row numbers; dates stay Excel serial numbers) |
| Download | `download <target> [--out DIR]` (default `/tmp/sharepoint-dl`, 50 MB cap) |
| Links | `link <target>` (web URL + existing sharing links) |
| Create sharing link | `link-create <target> [--type view\|edit] [--scope organization]` |
| Upload | `upload ./local.xlsx --to /Folder/ [--replace]` |
| Write cells | `cell-update <target> --sheet S --range B2:C3 --values '[["a",1],["b",2]]'` |
| Check connection | `test` |

## Requirements
- Browser with remote debugging at `${{config.cdp_url}}` and a signed-in **Teams** web tab (`teams.cloud.microsoft`) for `${{config.account}}`: the Graph token (Files/Sites scopes) is read from that tab's MSAL cache via CDP, no app registration. Needs `pip install websocket-client`. Reuses the `ms_teams` driver's auth helper. Expired tokens are renewed by reloading the Teams tab. If a command says "No Teams tab found"/"No unexpired token"/403, ask the user to open or refresh that tab; a 403 on a site may also mean the account has no access or the Teams token lacks the Sites scope (then use a sharing URL as target).

## Rules
- **Don't explore, everything is documented here.** Never run `--help`, `ls`/`find` for scripts, or read the watcher source; watcher scripts run only through `watch_script` (they live in `${{driver.watch_dir}}`). To validate a watch use `watch_script(..., dry_run=true)` and say clearly whether it was only a dry run or really registered.
- **Writes are real actions on `${{config.account}}`'s files**: `upload`, `cell-update` and `link-create` print a DRAFT (target, size, old vs new cell values, whether the file exists) unless `--yes` is given. Show the draft to the user, name the account and the exact target, and add `--yes` only after explicit approval. `--replace` and `--scope anonymous` (needs `--allow-anonymous`) need an explicit mention in the approval. Never upload/edit the App Register or other shared workbooks "to test"; tests go only to the user's own OneDrive.
- Bound scans: use `search` and `--top` instead of walking trees; read only needed files, use `--range` for big workbooks; save long text to `/tmp` and grep/summarize instead of pasting it.
- Typical use: find a workbook with `search "<name>"` then `read <ref> --sheets`; read meeting recordings/transcripts (`*.vtt`) with `ls /Recordings` and `read <ref> --timestamps`.

## Watchers (wake the session on change; do not poll files yourself)
Use `watch_script` with `script="sharepoint_watch.py"`, `integration="${{instance.name}}"` (injects this account's CDP URL/account) and `watcher=<id>`. Read-only: exit 0 silent / 200 changed / other = error; the first run is a silent baseline (existing files are not reported); wake text = NEW/CHANGED/DELETED, path, size, time, editor, link (never content). Schedule e.g. `cron:*/15 * * * *`, `retries=3`.

| watcher id | Fires on | Leading args | Extra flags |
|---|---|---|---|
| `sharepoint-folder` 📁 | new or changed files in a folder | `folder` | `--path /Recordings` `[--site S\|--drive D] [--recursive] [--new-only] [--name REGEX] [--ext vtt,docx] [--limit 10]` (scan capped at 500 files, 3 levels) |
| `sharepoint-file` 📄 | a given file got a new version | `file` | `--target <url\|driveId:itemId\|/path> [--site S\|--drive D]` |
| `sharepoint-site` 🗂️ | any change in a library (Graph delta) | `site` | `[--site S\|--drive D] [--path-prefix /Folder] [--name REGEX] [--ext x,y]` |

Pass only the extra flags in `args`. Example: `watch_script(session_id=<id>, script="sharepoint_watch.py", watcher="sharepoint-folder", integration="${{instance.name}}", args=["--path","/Recordings","--ext","vtt"], schedule="cron:*/15 * * * *", prompt="new recording transcript: summarize decisions/actions", retries=3)`.
